diff --git a/host/asm/phitop/view.md b/host/asm/phitop/view.md
index 88d0b01..1afdd3b 100644
--- a/host/asm/phitop/view.md
+++ b/host/asm/phitop/view.md
@@ -56,3 +56,13 @@ temperature, atoms, threads and the team's busy percent. Two lines so each fits
 frame's 132 columns. Measured with Intel-Phi-AmberMD's test simulation (48,668 argon atoms,
 120 threads on card 0): 2.9 to 3.4 steps/s and 311 to 321 ms a step against the program's own
 3.05 to 3.22 steps/s, team busy 83.3 to 85.0 % against its 80.5 to 84.8 %.
+
+## The worker's DMA channel on the pcie line (2026-11-06)
+
+When the co-processor worker's line is present (`DV_VPU_HAVE`), the pcie
+line starts with `card dma in X, out Y`: the bytes a second the worker
+moved with its own DMA channel (Intel-Phi-AVX-512-C `card/vpu/cdma.S`,
+channel 7: request pulls and result pushes), then `host dma to card` and
+the daemon's own counters as before. The daemon's `Traffic` counters
+never see that channel, which is card-owned; it goes first so a narrow
+terminal (`v_cols`, 132 in batch frames) keeps it.
